{{!-- /the-faith-received/transparency/ — what artificial intelligence
     did here, what we do about it, and the full list of works that
     carry a machine translation.

     The list is built client-side from the same catalogues the rest of
     the library uses, by faith-transparency.js. Fourteen thousand
     titles are not something to ship as markup, and a list generated
     at build time would go stale the moment a collection moved. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/browse/">Library</a></p>
      <h1>Our Commitment to Transparency</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">What artificial intelligence did here, what we do to keep it honest, and every work it touched.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-feature-body">
    <div class="container container-narrow faith-tp">

      <p class="faith-tp-lede">We understand the gravity of a project like The Faith Received. It is no light thing to publish nearly 70,000 primary sources of the Christian faith in one place, over 2,000 of which are translated into English for the first time. A project of this scope and scale never would have been possible without the help of artificial intelligence.</p>

      <p>But we are not ignorant of the promises and the perils of using this technology in this way. It matters that the quality of these translations is good, not that they simply exist. Which is why we do not see The Faith Received as a static resource, but as a living project, and one that requires radical transparency and openness to iteration.</p>

      <p>With that in mind, we have undertaken seven steps to ensure transparency and ongoing improvement of quality.</p>

      {{!-- Numbered as an ordered list rather than as prose with
            digits in it, so a screen reader announces seven steps and
            says which one it is on. --}}
      <ol class="faith-tp-steps">
        <li>
          <h2>Everything translated by artificial intelligence says so</h2>
          <p>Every machine-translated work carries a Translation Transparency panel at the top of the page. It names the language the text was translated from, before the text rather than in a footnote after it.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>The original is always beside the translation</h2>
          <p>Every machine-translated work carries the English, the original language, and, where the source digitised one, the page scan the original was read from. All three are in the Text Tools menu on every work, so anyone can check a sentence against the page it came from.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Anyone can report a problem</h2>
          <p>Every work has a Report An Issue button in the same menu. Reports go to an inbox that is reviewed. Works are updated as deemed appropriate.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>The reports are counted in public</h2>
          <p>Each work shows how many issues have been reported against it and how many have been settled.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Every correction is dated and published</h2>
          <p>When a work is corrected, what changed is written into that work's own history with the date. A translation that changes silently is worse than one that was wrong, because a reader who checked it once has no way to know it moved.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>A translation committee is being formed</h2>
          <p>We are assembling credentialed translators to begin checking these works and making the changes their reading calls for.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2>Every work says where it stands</h2>
          <p>Works carry a status of Reviewed or Needs Review. Until a translator has read a work, it says Needs Review, because silence has to mean nobody has checked this and never that it is fine. A reviewed work should be trusted further than one that has not been.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <p class="faith-tp-act">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-report-issue>Report an issue</button>
      </p>

      {{!-- The list. Closed by default: it runs to thousands of
            titles, and a reader who wants it will open it. --}}
      <section class="faith-tp-list-wrap" data-faith-transparency>
        <details class="faith-tp-list">
          <summary class="faith-tp-list-head">
            <span class="faith-tp-list-title">Every work carrying a machine translation</span>
            <span class="faith-tp-list-count" data-tp-count>Counting&hellip;</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faith-tp-list-body">
            <p class="faith-tp-list-note" data-tp-note></p>
            <ol class="faith-tp-works" data-tp-works></ol>
            <div class="faith-tp-more">
              <button type="button" class="bsearch-more" data-tp-more hidden>Show more</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

    </div>
  </section>

</main>


